# Expectation record for 08_gcc_extensions/004_case_ranges.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 004_case_ranges
area               = 08_gcc_extensions
description        = Case ranges in switch labels, over buckets, hexadecimal classes and a fallthrough group
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_audit_flags     = -Wall -Wextra -Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow -Werror
ub_notes           <<END
No two case ranges overlap and no range overlaps a single label, so no switch has a
duplicated case value.  Every selector is an initialized int, every accumulator stays
inside the range of int, and each switch is driven once by a constant and once from
volatile storage.  No header is included and printf is declared by hand, so nothing here depends on a
standard-library header bcc does not ship.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
The warning gate drops -pedantic for this program.  The subject under test is a GCC
extension, which is by definition not standard C, and -pedantic exists precisely to reject
such constructs: with it in force the program could not be compiled at all and the feature
would go untested, which constraint C3 forbids.  Every other member of the gate is
retained, including -Werror, so no other class of defect in this program is downgraded.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
cr_bucket_neg=10
cr_bucket_b1=10
cr_bucket_b2=10
cr_bucket_b3=1
cr_bucket_b4=10
cr_bucket_default=20
cr_hex_digit=7
cr_hex_lower=14
cr_hex_upper=11
cr_hex_none=-1
cr_single_hit=42
cr_single_miss=0
cr_fall_low=11
cr_fall_mid=10
cr_fall_high=100
cr_fall_none=0
cr_runtime_bucket=2
cr_runtime_hex=12
END

expected_divergence.id       = XD-GCCEXT-CASE-RANGES-001
expected_divergence.class    = compile_failure
expected_divergence.scope    = oracle_a; all targets; all opt levels
expected_divergence.basis    = docs/project-guide.md, the GCC extension inventory enumerates __attribute__, statement expressions, typeof, computed goto and inline assembly, and omits case ranges
expected_divergence.observed <<END
The documented extension inventory does not list case ranges among the GCC
extensions the frontend accepts, so a compile failure on a case-range label is
traceable to that documented gap rather than to an unexplained defect.  The
reference compiler accepts the construct and prints the stdout recorded below.
The program is written and executed regardless, because constraint C3 forbids
excluding a feature merely because it may be unimplemented; if the divergence does
not occur, this marker is stale and must be retired.
END
